WEBVTT

00:16.220 --> 00:17.930
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:18.560 --> 00:21.390
Damn it! Isagi won?

00:21.480 --> 00:25.600
Then let's choose our positions starting with the winner, Isagi-kun.

00:25.690 --> 00:27.480
I want to be a forward.

00:30.280 --> 00:35.280
<i>The first selection will be a tournament between the 5 teams in the same building.</i>

00:35.360 --> 00:38.080
The two teams with the highest scores will advance,

00:38.160 --> 00:41.080
while the rest will be eliminated from Blue Lock.

00:41.160 --> 00:42.870
Eliminated players will never again

00:42.960 --> 00:46.250
be able to play for the Japanese national team.

00:46.330 --> 00:47.420
However,

00:47.500 --> 00:49.300
from the 3 eliminated teams,

00:49.380 --> 00:52.720
<i>the players who scored the most goals will not be eliminated.</i>

00:52.800 --> 00:55.800
<i>If there is more than one player with the most goals,</i>

00:55.890 --> 00:57.760
<i>fair play points will be checked,</i>

00:57.850 --> 01:00.970
<i>and the player with fewer penalty points will continue.</i>

01:01.560 --> 01:04.230
<i>Your own goals, or your team's victory?</i>

01:04.310 --> 01:08.400
<i>Your decisions as a forward will be tested here.</i>

01:08.480 --> 01:12.610
This is a battle about creating soccer from scratch.

01:12.690 --> 01:17.200
<i>The first match will be in two hours, between Team X and Team Z.</i>

01:17.280 --> 01:18.320
Alright guys.

01:18.410 --> 01:20.830
We'll play with this formation in the first match.

01:20.910 --> 01:24.080
Let's win with center forward Isagi-kun as our base.

01:24.160 --> 01:25.290
Understood.

01:25.370 --> 01:28.460
Can we win by basing on Isagi, who is ranked pretty low?

01:28.540 --> 01:30.420
Shut up, Igaguri.

01:30.500 --> 01:32.760
I don't want to stay in defense, you know.

01:32.840 --> 01:34.550
As long as we win, right?

01:34.630 --> 01:35.880
I'm not complaining.

01:35.970 --> 01:38.590
"As long as we win", is that so?

01:38.680 --> 01:40.430
Can you even play goalkeeper?

01:40.510 --> 01:42.850
I just lost at rock-paper-scissors, that's all.

01:43.850 --> 01:46.520
<i>When he said 'a battle to create soccer from zero',</i>

01:46.600 --> 01:48.190
<i>what did he mean?</i>

01:48.270 --> 01:49.810
It's about time.

01:52.730 --> 01:57.820
<i>The Blue Lock match that will change my life is about to begin.</i>

02:00.700 --> 02:02.330
BUILDING 5, CENTRAL AREA

02:02.410 --> 02:04.410
Team X has arrived.

03:43.500 --> 03:47.000
CHAPTER 3: SOCCER'S 'ZERO'

03:47.640 --> 03:53.190
<i>All fouls in the first selection will be decided by the VAR system.</i>

03:53.850 --> 03:57.730
<i>The first match of Building 5, consisting of two 45-minute halves,</i>

03:57.820 --> 04:00.740
<i>Team X vs Team Z, let the match begin.</i>

04:01.400 --> 04:03.360
Scared, Isagi?

04:04.370 --> 04:07.620
Let's have as much fun as possible, otherwise we can't win.

04:09.410 --> 04:10.410
Okay.

04:13.500 --> 04:16.380
<i>He's right, I don't need to be scared.</i>

04:16.460 --> 04:19.840
<i>After all, I'm at the very bottom of the rankings, 274th.</i>

04:19.920 --> 04:21.050
<i>I just need to play and</i>

04:21.630 --> 04:22.760
<i>rise up!</i>

04:26.050 --> 04:29.180
<i>Should we pass back and attack again?</i>

04:32.980 --> 04:35.060
Hey! What are you doing, Raichi?

04:35.150 --> 04:38.320
There was a rule that the top scorer wins, right?

04:38.400 --> 04:40.190
I don't give a damn about the team.

04:40.280 --> 04:42.400
I'll do this my own way.

04:42.490 --> 04:44.610
You know your stuff, Raichi.

04:47.830 --> 04:49.620
If that's the rules here,

04:49.700 --> 04:52.710
I'll play for myself without any hesitation.

04:52.790 --> 04:56.330
Kunigami, looks like we'll get along well.

04:56.420 --> 04:57.330
What are you doing?

04:57.420 --> 04:58.460
Pass it to me too!

04:58.540 --> 05:00.300
Wait, what happened to our positions?

05:00.380 --> 05:01.300
Get out of my way!

05:01.380 --> 05:02.510
On your way.

05:02.590 --> 05:03.800
Damn.

05:03.880 --> 05:07.220
Your physique isn't bad.

05:08.220 --> 05:09.500
It's my lucky day.

05:10.560 --> 05:12.430
Look ahead.

05:13.680 --> 05:15.810
<i>They can't get along either?</i>

05:20.400 --> 05:22.440
<i>What's going on here?</i>

05:22.530 --> 05:26.660
<i>These idiots are only thinking about themselves.</i>

05:26.740 --> 05:30.780
This is a battle to recreate soccer.

05:31.540 --> 05:34.790
<i>That 'creating from zero' that guy talked about</i>

05:34.870 --> 05:37.250
<i>was this kind of dogfight?</i>

05:38.130 --> 05:39.670
<i>This isn't soccer.</i>

05:40.540 --> 05:41.920
<i>What should I do?</i>

05:42.000 --> 05:44.510
<i>Should I join them too?</i>

05:51.010 --> 05:52.010
<i>He slipped through!</i>

05:52.720 --> 05:54.350
If you don't get out of my way

05:55.730 --> 05:56.730
I'll kill you.

05:58.400 --> 06:00.810
TEAM X - BL RANK 250, BAROU SHOUEI

06:01.860 --> 06:02.860
<i>I'll stop him!</i>

06:03.570 --> 06:04.690
<i>He's coming. Is he going left?</i>

06:05.650 --> 06:06.950
<i>A chip shot?</i>

06:07.030 --> 06:08.360
<i>Damn, he got past me!</i>

06:08.450 --> 06:10.620
Sorry, Kuon. It's coming to you!

06:11.530 --> 06:13.660
-Leave it to us!
-No problem, two on one.

06:16.830 --> 06:18.370
<i>Two nutmegs in a row?</i>

06:18.460 --> 06:19.710
<i>What the hell is this guy?</i>

06:19.790 --> 06:21.340
<i>He's both huge and skilled!</i>

06:23.710 --> 06:24.840
<i>I couldn't even react.</i>

06:29.050 --> 06:32.350
Get it through your heads, you talentless bastards.

06:33.220 --> 06:36.430
The ball is not my 'friend' or anything.

06:37.730 --> 06:41.110
It's just a round slave that makes me stand out!

06:42.020 --> 06:45.480
I am the king of the field.

06:46.280 --> 06:50.200
<i>Can we win against someone like this?</i>

06:50.280 --> 06:52.280
-Awesome!
-Well done, King Barou!

06:52.370 --> 06:53.770
Aren't you the goalkeeper, dammit?

06:53.830 --> 06:54.910
Do your job properly!

06:54.990 --> 06:57.660
I've never been a goalkeeper before, what can I do?

06:57.750 --> 07:00.870
They only scored one goal, pull yourselves together.

07:00.960 --> 07:03.960
He's right. If we keep our positions and play with passes...

07:04.500 --> 07:06.320
If we do that, because you're the forward

07:06.380 --> 07:07.920
all the goals will be credited to you.

07:08.010 --> 07:10.260
The losers can go to defense.

07:10.340 --> 07:13.640
As soon as the ball comes to you, pass to me!

07:13.720 --> 07:15.850
Screw you, pass to me!

07:16.470 --> 07:18.560
-No, to me.
-No, pass to me!

07:18.640 --> 07:21.350
<i>Team Z, please continue the match.</i>

07:22.860 --> 07:24.190
<i>Calm down.</i>

07:24.270 --> 07:26.650
<i>The match just started.</i>

07:26.730 --> 07:29.070
<i>And what are they testing us on anyway?</i>

07:29.150 --> 07:31.570
<i>But whatever happens, I have to win.</i>

07:32.280 --> 07:34.660
<i>As long as the ball doesn't go to him...</i>

07:34.740 --> 07:37.490
Bachira! Let's advance by passing between us.

07:41.040 --> 07:42.920
Hey Igaguri, don't leave your position!

07:43.000 --> 07:46.380
Are you dumb, Isagi? The top scorer survives.

07:46.460 --> 07:48.630
You can only dream of getting a pass.

07:48.710 --> 07:51.260
-Better luck next time!
-Hey, wait!

07:51.340 --> 07:53.890
Now I understand the Blue Lock first selection.

07:53.970 --> 07:57.640
It's a battle where you score goals with only your own skills!

07:58.840 --> 07:59.770
Damn!

07:59.850 --> 08:00.980
Idiot, I stole the ball.

08:01.060 --> 08:02.940
Did you really lose it? I'll kill you!

08:02.940 --> 08:04.230
You fool, Igaguri!

08:04.310 --> 08:06.060
Everybody get back! We're defending!

08:06.150 --> 08:09.820
Hey, let's pass to Barou and support him.

08:09.900 --> 08:12.360
Don't you see their team play?

08:12.450 --> 08:15.780
If we win as a team rather than individual scores, there's no problem!

08:15.870 --> 08:17.330
You're right. Barou!

08:21.010 --> 08:22.210
Leave the right wing to me!

08:22.280 --> 08:23.240
I'll take the left!

08:23.290 --> 08:24.650
We'll leave the defense to you!

08:24.670 --> 08:27.590
<i>We're screwed. They're starting to sync up.</i>

08:27.670 --> 08:29.550
Barou. Everyone mark Barou!

08:29.630 --> 08:31.140
You're saying that, Igaguri?

08:31.160 --> 08:32.480
Damn. We have to stop him!

08:34.890 --> 08:39.260
Does it make sense for all you losers to crowd around me?

08:41.270 --> 08:42.640
<i>This won't work.</i>

08:42.700 --> 08:43.850
<i>If we leave Barou alone,</i>

08:43.940 --> 08:46.610
<i>he'll tear through our defense. But if we only focus on him,</i>

08:46.690 --> 08:49.320
-Come to that open space!
<i>-the other players will be free!</i>

08:49.400 --> 08:50.980
Catch it, Iemon!

08:52.780 --> 08:55.280
Hell yeah! That's the second!

08:55.360 --> 08:57.240
Thanks, King Barou!

08:57.320 --> 09:00.830
<i>We're screwed. At this rate we'll lose.</i>

09:00.910 --> 09:03.160
<i>They managed to become a team!</i>

09:03.250 --> 09:08.880
We lost the ball because of you, Igaguri!

09:03.250 --> 09:08.880
<i>But we can't even get along yet. We can't win like this.</i>

09:08.960 --> 09:11.340
I can't stand this anymore!

09:12.010 --> 09:15.180
<i>Until just a moment ago, they were in disarray too.</i>

09:15.880 --> 09:17.930
<i>Because of him.</i>

09:18.010 --> 09:21.930
<i>Barou's goal united them!</i>

09:22.640 --> 09:26.310
This is the battle to create soccer from zero.

09:28.730 --> 09:31.320
<i>If that dogfight is 'zero',</i>

09:31.400 --> 09:34.780
<i>then Barou's breathtaking play is 'one'.</i>

09:34.860 --> 09:35.700
One more!

09:35.780 --> 09:38.990
<i>Then, around this 'one', a strategy to win is formed,</i>

09:39.070 --> 09:41.490
<i>and a team emerges.</i>

09:41.580 --> 09:45.210
<i>Was that the meaning of 'creating soccer from zero'?</i>

09:46.870 --> 09:50.460
<i>If that's the case, we're done for.</i>

09:51.800 --> 09:56.470
<i>As the score gap widens, they're thinking more about themselves.</i>

09:56.550 --> 10:00.260
<i>In this situation, there's no one who can turn 'zero' into 'one'.</i>

10:01.010 --> 10:04.600
<i>Moreover, the opposing team's bonds are getting tighter.</i>

10:04.680 --> 10:06.230
<i>It's impossible now.</i>

10:06.810 --> 10:08.310
<i>We've already</i>

10:14.900 --> 10:17.820
<i>lost this match.</i>

10:20.700 --> 10:24.330
Ah, all we're doing is running around.

10:24.410 --> 10:27.120
It's impossible to score 5 goals in 3 minutes.

10:27.210 --> 10:31.340
But maybe we can score one, you and me.

10:32.500 --> 10:33.460
Bachira.

10:34.380 --> 10:38.800
The opponents have let their guard down being 5-0 up. It might be a one-time chance.

10:41.140 --> 10:42.140
You in?

10:44.720 --> 10:45.720
I'm in.

10:47.100 --> 10:51.520
<i>I'll turn this team's 'zero' into 'one'!</i>

11:00.990 --> 11:03.080
I'll draw them to me.

11:03.160 --> 11:05.370
Then I'll send a long pass to you, and you'll finish.

11:05.450 --> 11:06.910
Run, Isagi.

11:07.000 --> 11:08.160
Towards the goal.

11:08.250 --> 11:10.120
Okay, Bachira.

11:13.250 --> 11:14.540
<i>I'll score that goal!</i>

11:14.630 --> 11:15.800
What? Isagi-kun?

11:16.960 --> 11:18.550
<i>Even if turning back is impossible,</i>

11:18.630 --> 11:20.340
<i>if someone scores a goal,</i>

11:20.430 --> 11:22.590
<i>we can become a team around that person.</i>

11:22.680 --> 11:25.310
<i>It means we'll turn 'zero' into 'one'.</i>

11:25.390 --> 11:26.560
Surround him!

11:26.640 --> 11:28.520
<i>Together with Bachira, I'll score that goal.</i>

11:28.600 --> 11:31.690
<i>I'm sure this is the key to winning the next match.</i>

11:31.770 --> 11:33.770
So that's it, Isagi.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.940
<i>I'll be the light of Team Z!</i>

11:36.530 --> 11:37.440
<i>Right on target.</i>

11:37.440 --> 11:40.000
-Yes.
-Nice pass, Bachira.

11:41.280 --> 11:43.030
<i>One on one.</i>

11:43.120 --> 11:44.910
<i>I'll shoot!</i>

11:44.990 --> 11:46.830
Hey, number 11.

11:46.910 --> 11:48.290
Don't steal my light.

11:50.330 --> 11:52.620
I said I'm the king.

11:53.250 --> 11:55.710
Get past me if you can, loser.

11:55.790 --> 11:58.420
<i>Why is he here? Did he figure out our plan?</i>

11:58.510 --> 12:00.340
<i>What should I do? Should I try to get past?</i>

12:00.420 --> 12:01.590
<i>But against him...</i>

12:03.090 --> 12:05.510
<i>In a situation like this, what would a forward do?</i>

12:06.300 --> 12:08.060
Isagi! I'm behind you!

12:08.140 --> 12:09.720
Pass to me!

12:09.810 --> 12:11.390
-I'll shoot!
-I'm here!

12:11.480 --> 12:13.060
<i>Should I pass? No.</i>

12:13.690 --> 12:14.770
<i>This is my battle!</i>

12:14.860 --> 12:16.730
<i>If I'm going to survive Blue Lock,</i>

12:16.820 --> 12:18.820
<i>if I'm going to live as a forward...</i>

12:38.170 --> 12:40.090
Nice pass, Isagi.

12:40.170 --> 12:42.050
It's impossible to shoot from that distance.

12:56.520 --> 12:57.900
That's it!

13:00.190 --> 13:03.070
I passed involuntarily.

13:03.150 --> 13:06.910
What do you think you're doing, Isagi? Why did you pass to Kunigami?

13:06.990 --> 13:09.280
Compared to him, I was more open!

13:09.370 --> 13:12.410
No, I was planning to shoot.

13:13.160 --> 13:15.010
But for some reason, my body on its own...

13:15.080 --> 13:19.790
Are you an idiot, man? What's the point of passing when you could shoot?

13:21.000 --> 13:22.420
Don't, Raichi!

13:22.510 --> 13:23.800
We scored a goal anyway!

13:23.880 --> 13:25.840
Ha! Are you stupid too?

13:25.930 --> 13:27.300
After someone else scores,

13:27.390 --> 13:29.850
and on top of that losing 5-1, what's there to be happy about?

13:29.930 --> 13:31.430
You heard the rules, right?

13:31.510 --> 13:34.550
At the end of the day, the top scorer will win!

13:34.650 --> 13:36.810
But you wasted that chance and passed!

13:36.910 --> 13:40.070
What the hell did you come here for!

13:40.150 --> 13:41.150
I don't know.

13:41.230 --> 13:43.440
Because I made that pass involuntarily.

13:44.530 --> 13:45.900
Hey, number 11.

13:47.610 --> 13:51.370
Someone who gets scared in front of the goal can't be a forward.

13:52.080 --> 13:54.450
You're just talentless.

14:01.420 --> 14:02.550
<i>Time's up.</i>

14:02.630 --> 14:07.720
<i>Blue Lock Building 5 first match, ended with Team X's 5-1 victory.</i>

14:12.010 --> 14:13.430
<i>What am I doing?</i>

14:14.350 --> 14:17.060
<i>Wasn't I going to turn 'zero' into 'one'?</i>

14:23.610 --> 14:24.570
<i>Am I</i>

14:25.570 --> 14:27.400
<i>a failure as a forward?</i>

14:29.660 --> 14:33.240
Making Isagi the center forward was a mistake from the start!

14:33.330 --> 14:35.700
Next match, I'll be it!

14:35.790 --> 14:39.170
No, I'll be it. If I'm center forward, we can win.

14:39.250 --> 14:42.130
By the way, I'm not playing defense again.

14:42.210 --> 14:43.840
Trash should shut up.

14:43.920 --> 14:47.050
You're the trash Isagi didn't pass to.

14:47.130 --> 14:48.380
You wanna fight, punk?

14:49.380 --> 14:53.560
Someone who gets scared in front of the goal can't be a forward.

14:54.180 --> 14:56.180
<i>You're talentless.</i>

14:57.850 --> 14:59.480
<i>Why did I pass?</i>

15:00.150 --> 15:03.820
<i>Since I came here, I still haven't changed.</i>

15:03.900 --> 15:09.920
<i>What am I missing to survive Blue Lock as a forward?</i>

15:10.430 --> 15:11.820
-Pass to me!
-No, to me!

15:11.910 --> 15:13.740
-Pass to me too!
-Pass to me first.

15:13.830 --> 15:15.540
Cut it out already!

15:17.450 --> 15:18.660
Kuon.

15:18.750 --> 15:20.960
Don't you realize the situation?

15:21.040 --> 15:23.630
We've already lost once.

15:25.340 --> 15:29.590
In the first selection, every team will play against each other,

15:29.670 --> 15:31.800
and only 2 teams will advance.

15:32.550 --> 15:34.590
<i>Assuming each team wins two matches and loses two,</i>

15:34.610 --> 15:37.560
<i>everyone would have 6 points.</i>

15:37.640 --> 15:40.560
<i>That means the points we need to win</i>

15:40.640 --> 15:42.730
<i>is above that, 7.</i>

15:42.810 --> 15:46.070
<i>That will be the threshold determining who advances.</i>

15:46.150 --> 15:48.280
So if we lose twice,

15:48.360 --> 15:51.150
our elimination is only a matter of time.

15:51.240 --> 15:55.410
We've already reached the point of "if we lose again, we're done".

15:55.490 --> 15:57.990
If we don't plan how to win,

15:58.080 --> 15:59.620
we'll really be finished.

16:01.670 --> 16:04.130
Do you at least have a good plan?

16:04.210 --> 16:06.460
No, not yet.

16:06.540 --> 16:08.800
What the hell? You're all talk.

16:08.880 --> 16:11.470
-But this way-
-There's a way.

16:11.550 --> 16:15.930
I couldn't have scored that goal without Bachira and Isagi.

16:16.010 --> 16:17.510
That could be a hint to winning.

16:17.600 --> 16:22.020
Don't mess with me, musclehead! You just want to be the top scorer!

16:22.100 --> 16:23.480
But it was amazing.

16:24.600 --> 16:27.650
It was definitely the goal of the day.

16:27.730 --> 16:30.110
-You're naked!
-If we do this a lot, we can win.

16:30.190 --> 16:32.700
Right, Isagi? Right?

16:33.360 --> 16:34.660
Bachira.

16:34.740 --> 16:35.570
Are you dumb?

16:35.660 --> 16:37.740
We can't constantly pull off that perfect shot!

16:37.830 --> 16:40.540
Also, stop exposing yourself!

16:40.620 --> 16:41.710
But seriously,

16:41.790 --> 16:44.620
where have you seen a whole team made up of forwards?

16:44.710 --> 16:49.250
I don't think everything he said is correct.

16:49.340 --> 16:50.960
Chigiri.

16:51.050 --> 16:55.470
After all, even though Ego says it's to win the World Cup,

16:55.550 --> 16:59.930
he brought up the names Cristiano Ronaldo, Messi, and Cantona, but

17:00.020 --> 17:03.230
none of them won the World Cup.

17:05.520 --> 17:06.520
But still,

17:06.600 --> 17:10.900
the phrase 'a battle to create soccer from zero'

17:10.980 --> 17:14.490
I think might be a hint.

17:14.570 --> 17:15.910
Look, guys.

17:16.570 --> 17:19.030
Even though I don't know how we'll win yet,

17:19.120 --> 17:23.250
I think I've understood soccer's 'zero'.

17:24.250 --> 17:26.580
Spit it out, you talentless guy.

17:26.670 --> 17:32.420
In that match, at the beginning, because everyone was thinking only of their own goal,

17:32.510 --> 17:34.510
it was just like a dogfight.

17:35.260 --> 17:38.510
<i>I think that situation reflected 'zero'.</i>

17:38.600 --> 17:41.060
<i>Like you said, you couldn't really call it soccer.</i>

17:41.140 --> 17:42.270
<i>You're right.</i>

17:42.350 --> 17:46.940
What broke that 'zero' was Barou's goal.

17:47.020 --> 17:48.480
<i>With the impact of that play,</i>

17:48.560 --> 17:53.280
<i>the path to goal was illuminated and they started playing as a team.</i>

17:53.360 --> 17:59.120
<i>Barou, with his own talent, turned that dogfight that equated to 'zero' into 'one'.</i>

17:59.200 --> 18:01.790
Based on that,

18:01.870 --> 18:05.120
a team can evolve into '10' or even '100'.

18:05.210 --> 18:09.500
So what we need is the power to bring forth that 'one'.

18:09.580 --> 18:12.630
<i>And that's possible with an irresistible ego and talent.</i>

18:13.420 --> 18:16.630
If forwards are those who turn 'zero' into 'one',

18:16.720 --> 18:21.050
then are the other positions those who turn 'one' into 'ten' or 'a hundred'?

18:21.140 --> 18:24.430
So is it that Ego set up a system

18:24.520 --> 18:28.770
where the top scorer can survive for us to understand this?

18:28.850 --> 18:30.190
I think so.

18:30.270 --> 18:34.360
Because of that rule, we, experiencing an ego explosion,

18:34.440 --> 18:37.320
cast aside our positions and tactics,

18:37.400 --> 18:41.660
and were driven to think only about scoring.

18:42.490 --> 18:48.210
<i>As a result, without our egos colliding, it's impossible for us to become a team.</i>

18:49.420 --> 18:50.580
<i>Soccer,</i>

18:50.670 --> 18:51.960
<i>Team,</i>

18:52.040 --> 18:54.310
<i>are created by an unstoppable forward.</i>

18:55.210 --> 18:57.670
<i>I'm sure that's what Ego was talking about.</i>

18:59.300 --> 19:01.850
<i>Yes, yes. You made a good point.</i>

19:01.930 --> 19:04.680
<i>Hello there, diamonds in the rough.</i>

19:04.760 --> 19:08.140
The second match of your building has been completed.

19:08.230 --> 19:11.650
Team V defeated Team Y 8-0.

19:11.730 --> 19:13.520
What? 8-0?

19:14.150 --> 19:15.020
Wow.

19:16.730 --> 19:19.030
You're on the right track, but

19:19.110 --> 19:23.990
you don't seem to have grasped the part about turning 'zero' into 'one'.

19:24.080 --> 19:27.750
First, let's talk about Japan.

19:27.830 --> 19:30.420
Japanese people assign themselves tasks

19:30.500 --> 19:33.330
and take pleasure in completing those tasks.

19:33.420 --> 19:36.130
<i>For example, one of the few sports Japan can compete in globally,</i>

19:36.210 --> 19:38.670
<i></i>

19:38.760 --> 19:40.340
<i>Baseball.</i>

19:40.430 --> 19:43.090
<i>It has an inning system that separates offense and defense,</i>

19:43.180 --> 19:46.310
<i>and is a sport with no physical contact on the field.</i>

19:46.390 --> 19:49.600
<i>This sport, where everyone's role is clear,</i>

19:49.680 --> 19:53.400
<i>suits the Japanese personality perfectly.</i>

19:53.480 --> 19:54.860
<i>That's why we are strong.</i>

19:55.570 --> 19:57.570
But in soccer, things are different.

19:57.650 --> 19:59.820
<i>You are on an open field where offensive and defensive roles</i>

19:59.900 --> 20:01.910
<i>can change instantly.</i>

20:01.990 --> 20:03.600
<i>Moreover, there is a lot of physical contact.</i>

20:04.200 --> 20:09.540
<i>It's a sport you can't win just by fulfilling your assigned tasks.</i>

20:09.620 --> 20:13.210
That's why individual performances,

20:13.290 --> 20:15.750
individual talent, is necessary.

20:15.840 --> 20:18.760
These days, the positions that Japanese soccer can be proud of

20:18.840 --> 20:21.630
are midfielders and full-backs.

20:22.220 --> 20:23.800
They work like dogs for the team,

20:23.890 --> 20:26.760
turning the forward's 'one' into 'a hundred'.

20:26.850 --> 20:29.020
<i>Without the sacrifice of these players,</i>

20:29.100 --> 20:32.730
<i>Japanese soccer wouldn't have even come this far.</i>

20:32.810 --> 20:35.360
And moreover, there would be no revolution.

20:36.650 --> 20:40.990
So, diamonds in the rough, review your mindset.

20:41.070 --> 20:47.030
Scoring a goal in soccer means shattering the structure of the opposing team.

20:47.120 --> 20:49.450
In other words, forwards are destroyers.

20:49.540 --> 20:52.120
<i>Scoring a goal is the pinnacle of revolution</i>

20:52.210 --> 20:54.170
<i>that disrupts your opponent's order.</i>

20:54.250 --> 20:56.170
Diamonds in the rough,

20:56.250 --> 20:59.130
don't let the roles restrict you!

20:59.210 --> 21:01.630
<i>To turn 'zero' into 'one',</i>

21:05.680 --> 21:07.800
arm yourselves, forwards!

21:07.890 --> 21:09.140
Discover it.

21:09.220 --> 21:11.770
Discover the weapon that will tear your opponents apart

21:11.850 --> 21:14.600
and bring destruction!

21:14.690 --> 21:19.440
Think hard about what you can do with that body and mind of yours!

21:19.520 --> 21:23.780
<i>It's you and your weapons that will bring about the revolution called a goal!</i>

21:24.700 --> 21:27.490
<i>Victory follows after that.</i>

21:35.080 --> 21:36.210
<i>Weapon.</i>

21:36.290 --> 21:40.000
<i>What we need to win this first selection.</i>

23:11.840 --> 23:14.430
<i>Blue Lock, Extra Time!</i>

23:15.010 --> 23:17.850
A DAY IN BLUE LOCK

23:17.930 --> 23:18.770
WAKING UP

23:18.850 --> 23:20.600
Morning, Bachira.

23:20.690 --> 23:24.650
MEGURU BACHIRA, YOICHI ISAGI

23:24.730 --> 23:28.280
Pass it, King Kazu.

23:28.360 --> 23:30.240
WARM-UP AND TRAINING

23:30.320 --> 23:34.410
RENSUKE KUNIGAMI

23:34.490 --> 23:38.200
<i>Master of the training room, Kunigami Kinnikun!</i>

23:38.290 --> 23:39.710
TEAM TRAINING

23:39.790 --> 23:41.330
Ah! Muscle cramp!

23:41.400 --> 23:43.940
Damn it, that's the fifth one today.

23:43.970 --> 23:45.330
You're trying to slack off, right?

23:45.350 --> 23:47.630
No, it's definitely broken!

23:47.710 --> 23:51.050
It's like a muscle strain or a compound fracture!

23:51.130 --> 23:52.840
GURIMU IGARASHI

23:52.930 --> 23:54.850
Don't eat with your hands, dammit!

23:54.930 --> 23:58.180
So dirty! Use the chopsticks!

23:59.020 --> 24:00.890
Okay.

24:00.980 --> 24:03.770
Let's clean those hands, okay?

24:03.860 --> 24:05.150
Are you his mom?

24:05.230 --> 24:07.110
Mom Kuon!

24:07.190 --> 24:08.990
What are you doing, Chigiri?

24:09.070 --> 24:09.990
Hair care.

24:10.070 --> 24:11.200
HYOMA CHIGIRI

24:11.280 --> 24:12.780
What are you doing, Imamura?

24:12.860 --> 24:14.620
Skin care.

24:12.860 --> 24:15.620
YUDAI IMAMURA

24:15.700 --> 24:17.490
SLEEP TIME

24:20.370 --> 24:23.120
Are we sure he's asleep?

24:23.210 --> 24:25.590
Look at that face.

24:25.670 --> 24:28.130
I knew it wasn't broken.

24:28.210 --> 24:29.760
You lying bastard!